ppu_fs: the "[fs] open" line only with PS3_FSLOG, like the other per-call file traces.

cellFsOpen printed every successful open. Resistance 3 opens sound banks, level chunks and streamed data throughout
play, so the log fills with "[fs] open '/dev_hdd0/.../resident_sound.dat' -> fd 68" lines. stat, opendir and mkdir
already print only with PS3_FSLOG; open now does too. Failed opens and FS_CALLER output are unchanged.

Test: scripted run (boot, Continue, gameplay): no "[fs] open" lines without PS3_FSLOG; with it the same lines as before.

Upstream: not proposed yet.

---

diff --git a/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp b/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp
index 430de13..da178b1 100644
--- a/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp
@@ -320,3 +320,3 @@ static void cellFsOpen(ppu_context* ctx)
           } }
-      else fprintf(stderr, "[fs] open '%s' -> fd %d\n", gpath, fd); }
+      else if (getenv("PS3_FSLOG")) fprintf(stderr, "[fs] open '%s' -> fd %d\n", gpath, fd); }
     if (getenv("PS3_FSLOG_BT") && strstr(gpath, ".usm")) {
